      "result": "W",
      "result_description": "Wadebridge CC - 1st XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "36578",
      "match_notes": "Unbeaten Wadebridge moved to the top of the table with a second big win of the weekend, beating Gorran by 110 runs on the south coast. Inserted on a green but firm deck, openers Matt Jolliffe (72) and James Maycock (43) continued their prolific partnership with a third hundred stand of the summer, adding 133 for the first wicket before both fell to Robin Kendall (3-47). Jake Lakeman snared 2-40 at the death, but not without taking some punishment from the fluent Elliot Dunnett (44) and Neil Richards (29*) as Wadebridge amassed a strong 268-8. In reply, Gorran made steady progress through Rob Hurrell (29) and Kendall (23) before both fell to Charlie Ellis (2-39). After 20 overs the hosts were 3-down and just about up with the rate, but 4 wickets fell in 8 deliveries with the score on 99, including 3 in an over to Alek Gill (4-37). James Tomlinson made 20 but Cal Morse (2-5) made short work of the tail to have Gorran all out for 158 in the 34th over.",
